# After ship — Pulse and this tab

When this slot is **shipped**, close it. Then classify **this tab’s** next ask against Pulse (open slots, branches, dirty trees). Do not leave the slot open to ask “close it?”.

## When the slot is shipped

Two tracks. Both need the **human to have asked** to ship (finish / deploy / “push .cursor”). Agent-only commits (`sync_event.sh`, coordinator-state) do not close Pulse.

**Product** in this slot (`protocol.mdc` §4): every product repo is on `origin/main`, then every product service in the slot is deployed successfully — or the human declined deploy after `main`. Feature-branch-only push or a failed deploy does not close. If this project has no product deploy, `origin/main` for those repos is enough.

**Bus repos** — `.cursor`, `.coordinator`, and bus-only paths (`DATA_DIR` / `DOCS_DIR`). No product deploy. The human asked to push them, and that push landed on `origin/main` → `task_completed`. Do not offer deploy.

A **mixed** slot (product + bus): the product track wins. Pushing docs alone does not close while a product service in the slot is still undeployed.

Quiet *other* tasks still need a yes (`voice.mdc`). Auto-close is only for **this** slot after it ships.

## Same message, next ask

Ship and the next request may be one message. After `task_completed`, classify the **remainder** (or the next message in this tab). Read Pulse first (`parallel.mdc`).

| Next ask | Pulse |
|---|---|
| Thanks / “да” / “закрой” / no new work | Stay closed. One Coordinator line. Name other own live tasks if any. |
| More work on **this** shipped feature (missed bit, tweak) | **Reopen:** `task_started` with the **same** `task_id`, branch, services. Parallel check. If product repos sit on `main` and the feature branch is gone, recreate it from up-to-date `main`. |
| Explicit new bug / hotfix of something else | New FIX (`protocol.mdc` §2.1). Not the same `task_id`. |
| New planned work with a doc | Start per §2. |
| How / why / where, no edits | `research_started` (`research.mdc`). This tab is off-task after close. |
| Unclear | Ask. Do not start a slot or research. |

Reopen is not a new FIX slug. A distinct incident is a new FIX even in the same service.

```text
❌ Pushed .cursor as asked, then offered product deploy
✅ Pushed .cursor as asked; Pulse closed. No deploy.

❌ Deployed, then asked “close the slot?”
✅ Deployed; Pulse closed the task.

❌ “ещё то же самое” → new FIX-…
✅ More of the same feature → reopen the same task_id.

❌ “почему это не дошло…” after ship → new task
✅ Off-task how/why → research.

❌ “почини другой баг в том же сервисе” → reopen
✅ New FIX, parallel check.
```
